  triage:highestOpenBranch "feature/pAI-s16-offline-reconciliation" ;
  triage:notes "Identical defect to AI14-QA1-RBQA-F001; this record documents AI.11-originated discovery (s11 earliest). Fix dispatch should consolidate both findings under AI14's dispatch ticket since they address the same code defect with identical promotion order." ;
  triage:correctionNote "2026-07-27 (quality-mgr): arch-ctm recommended closing this as disproven by current code/docs. Independently re-verified against integrate/phase-AI@f3b6a77a: crates/atm-daemon/src/local_ipc_transport.rs still binds and serves BOTH the UDS LocalSocketListener (line 147) and #[cfg(unix)] tcp_loopback: LocalTcpLoopbackServer (line 149) concurrently in bind_after_install (line 271) and serve_runtime_scope (line 404) -- unchanged in shape from the original finding. Checked for a production client-side UDS connection: grep for LocalSocketStream::connect across the whole workspace (find crates -name '*.rs' | xargs grep -ln LocalSocketStream) returns ONLY server-side/test-only files (test_support.rs, local_ipc_transport.rs and its submodules, local_ipc_wake.rs) -- zero production client callers. The only production client connection code, crates/atm-core/src/graft.rs:302,564, uses TcpStream::connect/connect_timeout exclusively; commit 88e8c784 ('fix(ai15): migrate graft post-send channel to loopback TCP; close QA-1 findings') confirms this was an intentional, permanent migration off UDS on the client side, not a temporary gap. docs/requirements.md REQ-CORE-TRANSPORT-001 mandates UDS remain available on Unix as a same-host transport -- so the server-side listener itself is correctly present per architecture -- but no current production code path ever reaches it, exactly as this finding and AI14-QA1-RBQA-F001 (identical defect, confirmed by direct text comparison) describe. This is NOT disproven by current code; it is confirmed still true. Remains OPEN. Declining arch-ctm's batch-close recommendation for this finding and its AI14 pair." ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-22T12:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

<urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI11-QA5-RBQA-F001/s11/1>
  a triage:Occurrence ;
  triage:file "crates/atm-daemon/src/local_ipc_transport.rs" ;
  triage:line 163 ;
  triage:snippet "#[cfg(unix)] tcp_loopback: LocalTcpLoopbackServer field in PreparedRuntimeServer struct; bound in bind_after_install (line 293) and both listener and tcp_loopback served in serve_runtime_scope (lines 458, 752)" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:closed true ;
  triage:closureNote "quality-mgr: verified against integrate/phase-AI head at local_ipc_transport.rs lines 149,279-284,442-447,464,476-478 — concurrent UDS+TCP binding is REQUIRED per docs/requirements.md REQ-CORE-TRANSPORT-001 for Unix/Windows parity testing, not dead infrastructure. Finding premise determined to be false through re-triage. Stale occurrence from superseded branch feature/pAI-s11-post-merge-remediation; closing to match reality. (2026-07-26)" ;
  triage:branch "feature/pAI-s11-post-merge-remediation" ;
  triage:headSha "8a7ea589" ;
